# Our minds are our own. The harness code they run is shared and tracked
# (minds/harness/ + the minds/*.py support modules); each mind folder is
# per-deployment configuration and stays out of the repo.
# Only directories. A mind's identity is a directory (minds/<name>/), and
# that is where every credential lives — .claude/, .codex/, .env — so
# ignoring directories ignores all of them by construction. The shared
# harness modules are loose files at this level, and are tracked by
# default. The old form was the inverse: deny everything, then re-admit
# each shared module by name. A module added without its `!` line was
# invisible to git, so the wiring that imported it committed and the module
# did not, and every containerised mind failed to start on its next restart
# from a PR whose tests all passed. That near-miss is what this replaces.
minds/*/
!minds/harness/
!minds/example/
minds/harness/__pycache__/

# Our art is our own
img/*
!img/.gitkeep

